1. Find if we can combine all numbers through n-1 operations to get exactly 1
2. Each operation takes two numbers x,y, computes f(x+y), and replaces them with that result
3. f(x) = x if x not divisible by k, otherwise f(x) = f(x/k) (essentially removes trailing factors of k)
4. n ≤ 16, sum ≤ 2000 - this suggests search with memoization is feasible

