The problem requires finding the minimum budget to disconnect two towns s and t by removing at most 2 roads. My solution uses BFS to check connectivity after removing specific edges.

For each test case, I check:
1. If s and t are already disconnected (0 cost)
2. All single edges that, when removed, disconnect s and t (1 edge, 1 cost option)
3. All pairs of edges that, when removed together, disconnect s and t (2 edges, sum of costs)

The edges are enumerated, and for each candidate removal scenario, I build the graph without those edges and use BFS to verify if s can still reach t. I track the minimum total budget among all valid disconnection scenarios.

```python
def solution(input_str):
